 ## Overview
-The Geometric Structure-Aware Loss Function (GS Loss) is a classification loss designed for viewpoint estimation in volume rendering that modifies the standard Softmax loss by incorporating geometric constraints between neighboring viewpoints on the viewing sphere [S1]. Unlike standard Softmax, which treats all incorrect classes as equally wrong, GS Loss assigns non-zero weights to neighbor viewpoints based on their geodesic distance from the ground truth, explicitly exploiting the continuity and correlation inherent in spherical camera parameterizations [S1].
